    <DataNode elementId="AT2G04450-MONOMER" textLabel="NADH pyrophosphatase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9SJC4" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="635" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, dreher">NUDX6 is a member of the family of Nudix (nucleoside diphosphate linked to some moiety X) family of hydrolases. Subcellular localization prediction proteins indicate that NUDX6 is a cytosolic protein |CITS: [15878881]|. &lt;i&gt;In vitro&lt;/i&gt; assays originally highlighted the ability of this protein to act on |FRAME: ADENOSINE_DIPHOSPHATE_RIBOSE ADP-ribose|, but subsequent analyses of mutant plants indicated that NUDX6 plays a much more important role in regulating NADH levels and NADH/NAD+ ratios in Arabidopsis plants |CITS: [20181750][7829480]|. NUDX6 also appears to be involved in salicylic acid-mediated plant signaling and defense responses and its transcripts are preferentially expressed in the leaves |CITS: [20181750]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G04450-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT2G04450.1" />
